  "problem": "Compute the values of $\\theta \\in [0,\\pi )$ for which the polar curve $r=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ has a horizontal tangent, given that\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(\\theta )=-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ),\\,{y}^{′}(\\theta )=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ).\n$$\n\nIn **ascending order**, the polar curve has horizontal tangents at\n\n${\\theta }_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,{\\theta }_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}.",
